Brute Force Approach can be using --> First we square array and then we sort it
Optimal Approach can be using --> Two Pointers

## Input:
-4 -1 0 3 10

Output:
[0, 1, 9, 16, 100]

Brute
----------------------------
n = list(map(int, input().split()))
for i in range(len(n)):
    n[i] = n[i] ** 2
n.sort()
print(n)

TC:O(NlogN)
SC:O(1)


Optimal
--------------------------------------
n = list(map(int, input().split()))
result = [0] * len(n)
left = 0
right = len(n) - 1
k = len(n) - 1
while left <= right:
     if abs(n[left]) > abs(n[right]):
        result[k] = n[left] ** 2
        left += 1
    else:
        result[k] = n[right] ** 2
        right -= 1
    k -= 1
print(result)

TC:O(N)
SC:O(N) because result is required


Core pattern:
left  →        ← right
       ↓
compare absolute values
       ↓
put larger square at result[k]
       ↓
k--
